  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThis implementation follows the structure of the multi-phase optimization method but introduces several enhancements to potentially lower the objective score further. The algorithm consists of three main phases: global search, polishing, and targeted exploration. \n\nThe approach aims to:\n- Start with a normalized step function based on provided data\n- Use Adam optimization with improved hyperparameters to explore the solution space \n- Apply aggressive local search (coordinate descent) to refine the solution\n- Conduct targeted explorations on promising subspaces to find further improvements\n\nKey improvements from the baseline program include:\n- Better handling of non-negativity constraints \n- Improved gradient calculation using autograd's JIT compilation for speed\n- Thorough time management separating global search and local refinement\n- Structured fallback candidates when needed\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nThe objective function to minimize is:\n    score(seq) = 2 * n * max(||self(seq)**2||_\u221e) / (\u2211seq)^2\n\nwhere:\n- n = sequence length\n- self(seq) = full linear convolution of seq\n- ||x||_\u221e = sup norm of array x\n\nEach phase's specifications:\nGlobal search phase:\n- Use spectral initialization with time-domain constraints\n- Normalize to \u2211==\u221a(2*n)\n- Compute gradient via analytic formula: \n    \u2207_params = (\u03c0/(2\u03c4) * (FA_\u03c9 * \u00b0 / (r\u00b7\u03b8)) + \u03ba*(value-injective in energy domain))\n\nConstraints:\n- Non-negative values enforced via project_simplex\n- \u03c4 clipping between 0.01 and 0.1 ensures numerical stability\n- Gradient damping parameters (\u03b21=0.9, \u03b22=0.99) reduce noise\n\nPolishing phase (coordinate descent):\n- Implements structured neighborhood search with five types:\n  \u2022 Random single-element tuning\n  \u2022 Strategic pair transfers \n  \u2022 Block perturbations preserving sum\n  \u2022 Local center modifications\n  \u2022 Progressive smoothing to avoid sharp peaks\n- Uses explicit value history storage to detect lock-ins\n- Maintains separation between exploration and validation\n\nTargeted exploration phase:\n- Focuses on energy conservation across multiple time scales\n- Uses exponential similarity metrics to sample critical regions\n- L1 regularization to enforce sparsity\n- Chirp-based transformations for long-range pattern search\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nThe algorithm operates with explicit time budget management:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\nfrom autograd import ?\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize as scipy_minimize\n\ndef main_propose_candidate(seed=42, **kwargs):\n    # Initialize base sequence with available data\n    best_seq, best_score = initialize_sequence(**kwargs)\n    \n    # Evaluate initial performance\n    try_complete_steps = not bool(kwargs.get('partial_run', False'))\n    if try_complete_steps and evaluate_sequence(best_seq) is not np.inf:\n        first_score, _ = score_fast(best_seq)\n        best_score = min(best_score, first_score)\n        logger.log(f\"Initial score: {first_score}\")\n    \n    # Phase 1: Global search\n    n_values = [1024, 4096] if kwargs.get('scaling', 'auto')=='auto' else [1024]\n    alphas = [0.3, 0.5] if try_complete_steps else [0.5]\n    \n    phasewatch = time.time()\n    for n in n_values:\n        if time.time() - phasewatch > kwargs.get('max_time', 2400) \n            break\n        logger.log(f\"\\nPhase 1 for n={n}\")\n        seq = polar_sparse_representation(best_seq, n, kwargs['coeff_range'], **{k: v})\n        seq = enforce_constraints(seq)\n        \n        # Compute simplex projection\n        s_val = \u2211seq\n        norm_factor = np.sqrt(2*n) / s_val if s_val < 1e-10 else 1\n        seq *= norm_factor\n        \n        # Parallel optimization\n        adam_result = adam_optimization(seq, kwargs['time_limits']['adam'])\n        polished_candidate = coordinate_descent(adam_result, kwargs['time_limits']['polish'])\n        \n        # Verify freezing\n        if not is_converged(polished_candidate):\n            final_verify = evaluate_sequence(polished_candidate)\n            best_score = min(best_score, final_verify) if s_val < 0.01 else best_score\n            logger.log(f\"Final validated score: {final_verify}\")\n            best_seq = polished_candidate\n            \n        # Targeted exploration\n        elif try_complete_steps and kwargs['exploration_depth'] > 0:\n            targets = [150, 50]  # energy targets per length per run\n            logger.log(\"Phase 2: Targeted exploration\")\n            for t in targets:\n                seq = near_optimal_bridge(seq, t)\n                if is_enhancing(seq):\n                    score_val = score_fast(seq)\n                    if score_val < best_score:\n                        best_score = score_val\n                        logger.log(f\"Discovered score step: {score_val}\")\n    \n    # Phase 3: Multidimensional lock-in\n    logger.log(\"\\nPhase 3: Progressive dimensionality optimization\")\n    if try_complete_steps:\n        dimension_pruning = coord_dimension_pruning(best_seq)\n        final_seq = dimension_pruning.restore()\n        final_score = score_fast(final_seq)\n    else:\n        final_seq = best_seq\n    \n    # Lower fallback policies\n    multiple_fallback = []\n    for dim_adjust in range(3):\n        fallback = {} if dim_adjust == 0 else {k: v}\n        fallback_score = evaluate_sequence(final_seq)\n        if fallback_score < best_score or np.isinf(best_score):\n            best_score = fallback_score\n            best_seq = final_seq\n    \n    return best_seq, best_score\n```\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nThe algorithm includes:\n\n```python\n# Initialization strategies\nINIT_MODULES = {\n    'providing_bridge': (\n        lambda a, n, kwargs: (a * (n/a)**(0.9) if 'stretch' in kwargs else a \n                        ) if not hasattr(a, 'type') else a.astype(np.float64)\n    ),\n    'pseudorandom_bridge': (\n        lambda a, n5: ramp_init(n, kwargs['rng'], kwargs.get('bridge_style', 'ramp'))\n    ),\n    'energy_bridge': (\n        lambda a, n: pulse_init(n, kwargs['tau'], kwargs['width_param'])\n    )\n}\n\n# Exploration enhancements\nREFINEMENT_MODULES = {\n    'structure_refinement': (\n        policy: lambda w: self_convolve.best_pos * w / (1000+\u03b5) if weights.n > n0\n                else keep_widespread(w)\n    ),\n    'refactoring': (\n        lambda params, grad_weights: {\n            base_shift: params['shift'],\n            center_focus: params['center']\n        }\n    ),\n    'structured_walk': (\n        evolve: [\n            'single_ascending',\n            'pair_clockwise',\n            'array_exp']\n    )\n}\n\n# Core optimization parameters\nPARAM_SCALE = 14\nTAU_CLIP = (0.01, 0.1)\nCONV_CLIP = (0.001, 100/\u03b5)\nOPTIM_MULTIPLIER = 1.2\nTRAP_CHECK_INTERVAL = 3\n\n# Algorithmic variations\nPCA_ENABLED = kwargs.get('components', 0)\nSPAWN_COUNT = 5\n```\n\n5. Computational budget and robustness\nThe search:\n\n```python\n# Time management\nmax_time = kwargs.get('time_limits', 2400)\ntimelimit_adam = 1.5 * max_time * (1+PCA_ENABLED)/OPTIM_MULTIPLIER\ntimelimit_polish = 0.4 * max_time * (SPAWN_COUNT/SCALEFACTOR)\n\n# Scaling checks\nfor length in tqdm.tqdm([1024, 2048, 4096, ...], total_steps=):\n    if length > 4*1024 or computation_time > 0.9*timelimit_adam:\n        break\n    [execute Adam optimization for n, \u03a3\u2248\u221a(2n)] with gradient penalty\n    evaluation_cost = time_required \u2248 O(length^1.5)\n    expected_storage = memory_usage*n\n    if expected_storage > GAUTOMATH_MEMORY_LIMIT or time_remaining.length < 1:\n        fallback_sequence = lerp_simplex(current_best, length, p)\n        validate_candidate(fallback_sequence)\n        break\n```\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nStrict validation procedures:\n\n```python\ndef validate_candidate(seq):\n    try:\n        score_val = score_fast(seq)\n    except FloatingPointError or OverflowError:\n        score_val = float('inf')\n    if not is_finite(score_val) or array_has_invalid_elements(seq):\n        return None, float('inf')\n\nvalidator = lambda y, x: {\n    if np.isnan(y) or np.isinf(x): return np.inf\n    else: return compute_score(y)\n}[1]\n```\n\nFallback conditions:\n\n```python\nif not find_explicit_lower or time_insufficient:\n    fallback_candidates = [\n        build_half_step_seq(length**0.9),\n        generate_oscillatory(length, center_freq)\n    ]\n    for cand in fallback_candidates:\n        score_cand = evaluate_sequence(cand)\n        if is_valid:\n            current_best = cand\n            break\n    else:\n        basic_step = np.ones(length) / 1000\n        return basic_step, compute_score(basic_step)\n```",
